IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Taxation Administration Act 1953 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- the PAYG instalments I must pay in advance as a sole trader
-- (Schedule 1 Part 2-10, Division 45): whether I am liable (ss 45-15, 45-50), what kind of payer I am (ss 45-125, 45-130,
-- 45-132, 45-134, 45-140, 45-155), for which quarters (ss 45-50, 45-60, 45-125(2)) and by when (ss 45-61, 45-70), the rate and
-- the instalment on my instalment income (ss 45-1, 45-110), whether I must notify my instalment income (s 45-20), my credit
-- (s 45-30), and the general interest charge if I pay late (s 45-80; Part IIA ss 8AAC, 8AAD, 8AAE).
--
-- SEAT: the taxpayer -- an individual carrying on a business as a sole trader (Jake): "Must I pay tax in advance, how much, and
-- by when?" The Commissioner's acts (giving or withdrawing a rate, notifying notional tax) are asked as facts about what the
-- Commissioner has done.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 226, compilation date 27 August 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 79, 2026 and Act No. 82,
-- 2026), register id C2026C00393, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1953A00001.txt. THE FORMULAS ARE MISSING FROM
-- THE DEPOSIT: ss 45-110(1), 45-115(1)(a) and 45-320(1) end "as follows" or "using the formula:" and the text goes straight on.
-- Where a formula is needed it is taken from the Guide (s 45-1) and labelled INFERENCE. The Taxation Administration Regulations
-- 2017 set no number used here.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Notional tax and the instalment rate formula (ss 45-320 to 45-340), GDP adjustment (Subdivision 45-L),
-- benchmark tax (Subdivision 45-M), varying the rate (Subdivision 45-F, beyond s 45-110(2)(b)), the monthly payer test (s 45-138,
-- an INPUT), companies, trusts, partnerships and consolidated groups; the base interest rate (the Reserve Bank's published
-- 90-day Bank Accepted Bill yield, s 8AAD(2) -- an INPUT); remission of the charge (s 8AAG, the Commissioner's judgment).
--
-- Income years end on 30 June and are named by the calendar year in which they end (2029 is the 2028-29 income year).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Taxation Administration Act 1953 -- PAYG instalments`

§§ `ss 45-15, 45-50(4) -- am I liable to pay instalments at all`

-- s 45-15(1): "The Commissioner may give you an instalment rate from time to time, by giving you written notice of the rate."
-- (2): "You are liable to pay instalments under this Division if the Commissioner has given you an instalment rate." Note 2: "If
-- your assessable income has always consisted wholly of withholding payments ... the Commissioner will not give you an instalment
-- rate." s 45-50(4): liable only if "(a) the Commissioner has given you an instalment rate; and (b) the Commissioner has not
-- withdrawn your instalment rate before the end of that quarter, month or year." Business income does not by itself make anyone
-- liable.
@export Am I liable to pay PAYG instalments (ss 45-15, 45-50(4))?
GIVEN `the Commissioner has given me an instalment rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has given you written notice of an instalment rate
      `the Commissioner has withdrawn it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has withdrawn that rate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable to pay PAYG instalments` IF
    `the Commissioner has given me an instalment rate` AND (NOT `the Commissioner has withdrawn it`)

§§ `ss 45-125, 45-130, 45-132, 45-134, 45-140, 45-155 -- what kind of payer am I`

-- s 45-140(1): you may choose to pay annually "instead of quarterly" if, at the end of the starting instalment quarter, "(a) you
-- are neither registered, nor required to be registered, under Part 2-5 of the GST Act; and (b) you are not a partner in a
-- partnership that is registered, or required to be registered ...; and (c) your most recent notional tax notified by the
-- Commissioner is less than $8,000". ((d), (e) concern companies; (1A) is not modelled.) s 45-155(1)(a): an annual payer stops
-- being one if notified notional tax "is $8,000 or more".
@export May I choose to pay my PAYG instalments annually (s 45-140)?
GIVEN `I am registered or required to be registered for GST` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registered, or required to be registered, for GST
      `I am a partner in a GST-registered partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a partner in a partnership registered or required to be registered for GST
      `my most recent notional tax notified` IS A NUMBER @desc The most recent notional tax the Commissioner has notified to you, in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I choose to pay annually` IF
        (NOT `I am registered or required to be registered for GST`)
    AND (NOT `I am a partner in a GST-registered partnership`)
    AND `my most recent notional tax notified` LESS THAN 8000

-- s 45-130(1)(a): at the end of the starting instalment quarter, "you are an individual who is not an annual payer, a monthly payer
-- or a quarterly payer who pays on the basis of instalment income" -- a quarterly payer on GDP-adjusted notional tax. s
-- 45-125(1)(b): you may instead "choose to pay quarterly instalments on the basis of your instalment income". s 45-134(1): an
-- individual pays 2 instalments (third and fourth quarters, s 45-50(2)) if (a) carrying on a primary production business whose
-- base-year income exceeded the related deductions, or (b) a special professional whose base-year professional income exceeded
-- the related deductions; otherwise 4 (s 45-132). A monthly payer (s 45-138) is an INPUT.
DECLARE `Payer kind` IS ONE OF
    `a monthly payer`
    `an annual payer`
    `a quarterly payer on instalment income`
    `a quarterly payer paying 4 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax`
    `a quarterly payer paying 2 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax`

DECLARE `Me as an instalment payer` HAS
    `I meet the monthly payer requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am registered or required to be registered for GST` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a partner in a GST-registered partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my most recent notional tax notified` IS A NUMBER
    `I choose to pay annually` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I choose to pay on my instalment income` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a primary producer with a base-year profit from it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a special professional with a base-year profit from it` IS A BOOLEAN

@export What kind of PAYG instalment payer am I (ss 45-125, 45-130, 45-132, 45-134, 45-140)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me as an instalment payer` @desc Your registrations, notified notional tax, choices and kind of business
GIVETH A `Payer kind`
`What kind of instalment payer am I` MEANS
    IF `me`'s `I meet the monthly payer requirement` THEN `a monthly payer`
    ELSE IF `me`'s `I choose to pay annually`
            AND `May I choose to pay annually` (`me`'s `I am registered or required to be registered for GST`)
                                               (`me`'s `I am a partner in a GST-registered partnership`)
                                               (`me`'s `my most recent notional tax notified`)
         THEN `an annual payer`
         ELSE IF `me`'s `I choose to pay on my instalment income` THEN `a quarterly payer on instalment income`
              ELSE IF `me`'s `I am a primary producer with a base-year profit from it` OR `me`'s `I am a special professional with a base-year profit from it`
                   THEN `a quarterly payer paying 2 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax`
                   ELSE `a quarterly payer paying 4 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax`

§§ `ss 45-50, 45-60, 45-125(2) -- for which quarters am I liable`

-- s 45-60: the first instalment quarter "consists of the first 3 months of the income year"; the second, the fourth to sixth; the
-- third, the seventh to ninth; the fourth, the tenth to 12th. For an income year ending 30 June: 30 September, 31 December, 31
-- March and 30 June.
GIVEN `income year ending in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the income year ends
      `quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The instalment quarter, 1 to 4
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the instalment quarter` MEANS
    IF `quarter` EQUALS 1 THEN Date 30 9 (`income year ending in` MINUS 1)
    ELSE IF `quarter` EQUALS 2 THEN Date 31 12 (`income year ending in` MINUS 1)
         ELSE IF `quarter` EQUALS 3 THEN Date 31 3 `income year ending in`
              ELSE Date 30 6 `income year ending in`

-- s 45-50(1): liable for an instalment quarter if, at its end, a quarterly payer on instalment income or paying 4 instalments on
-- GDP-adjusted notional tax; (2): for "the third or fourth instalment quarter" only, if paying 2; (4): only while the rate stands.
-- s 45-125(2)(a): the starting instalment quarter is the one in which the rate is given for the first time, "even if it is not
-- the first instalment quarter" -- so nothing is due for a quarter that ended before the rate was given. Annual and monthly
-- payers pay otherwise (ss 45-50(2A), (3)).
@export Am I liable to pay an instalment for this quarter (ss 45-50, 45-125(2))?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Payer kind` @desc What kind of instalment payer you are
      `income year ending in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the income year ends
      `quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The instalment quarter, 1 to 4
      `the Commissioner has given me an instalment rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has given you an instalment rate
      `the day the rate was first given` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commissioner first gave you an instalment rate, ISO 8601
      `the Commissioner has withdrawn it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner withdrew the rate before the end of the quarter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable for an instalment for the quarter` IF
        `the Commissioner has given me an instalment rate`
    AND `the day the rate was first given` AT MOST `the last day of the instalment quarter` `income year ending in` `quarter`
    AND (NOT `the Commissioner has withdrawn it`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the kind`
         WHEN `a quarterly payer on instalment income` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a quarterly payer paying 4 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a quarterly payer paying 2 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax` THEN `quarter` AT LEAST 3
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `ss 45-61, 45-70 -- by when must I pay`

-- s 45-61(1): a quarterly instalment "is due on or before the 21st day of the month after the end of that quarter". (2): a deferred
-- BAS payer, "(c) the 28th day of the month after the end of that quarter unless all or a part of a December falls within the last
-- month of that quarter; or (d) if all or a part of a December falls within the last month of that quarter--the next 28 February."
@export By when must I pay my quarterly instalment (s 45-61)?
GIVEN `income year ending in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the income year ends
      `quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The instalment quarter, 1 to 4
      `I am a deferred BAS payer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a deferred BAS payer
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I pay my quarterly instalment` MEANS
    IF `I am a deferred BAS payer`
    THEN IF `quarter` EQUALS 2 THEN Date 28 2 `income year ending in` ELSE Date 28 (DATE_MONTH `end` PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR `end`)
    ELSE Date 21 (DATE_MONTH `end` PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR `end`)
    WHERE
        `end` MEANS `the last day of the instalment quarter` `income year ending in` `quarter`

-- s 45-70(2): "If the income year ends on 30 June, the [annual] instalment is due on or before the next 21 October."
@export By when must I pay my annual instalment (s 45-70(2))?
GIVEN `income year ending in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the income year ends (30 June)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I pay my annual instalment` MEANS
    Date 21 10 `income year ending in`

§§ `ss 45-1, 45-110 -- how much`

-- s 45-110(2): the applicable instalment rate is "(a) unless paragraph (b) or (c) applies--the most recent instalment rate given to
-- you by the Commissioner under section 45-15 before the end of that quarter; or (b) if you have chosen an instalment rate for that
-- quarter under section 45-205--that rate"; (c) a rate chosen for an earlier quarter of the year.
@export What instalment rate applies to me for the quarter (s 45-110(2))?
GIVEN `the Commissioner's most recent rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The most recent instalment rate the Commissioner gave you before the end of the quarter, in percent
      `I chose a rate under s 45-205` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you chose your own rate for the quarter (or an earlier quarter of the year)
      `the rate I chose` IS A NUMBER @desc The rate you chose, in percent
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What instalment rate applies to me` MEANS
    IF `I chose a rate under s 45-205` THEN `the rate I chose` ELSE `the Commissioner's most recent rate`

-- s 45-110(1): "Work out the amount of an instalment ... as follows" -- THE FORMULA IS MISSING FROM THE DEPOSIT. INFERENCE from the
-- Guide, s 45-1: "you must work out the amount of your quarterly instalment by multiplying your instalment income for an instalment
-- quarter by the rate the Commissioner gave you, or by a rate you choose yourself." s 45-120(1): instalment income "includes your
-- ordinary income derived during that period, but only to the extent that it is assessable income" -- an INPUT. The GDP-adjusted
-- instalment is the amount the Commissioner notifies (s 45-112(1)(a)) -- not computed.
@export How much is my quarterly instalment on my instalment income (s 45-1, INFERENCE for s 45-110(1))?
GIVEN `my instalment income for the quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc Your assessable ordinary income derived in the quarter, in dollars
      `the rate in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc The applicable instalment rate, in percent
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my quarterly instalment` MEANS
    `my instalment income for the quarter` TIMES `the rate in percent` DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `ss 45-20, 45-30 -- notifying my instalment income, and my credit`

-- s 45-20(1): if liable for an instalment "(even if it is a nil amount), you must notify the Commissioner of the amount of your
-- instalment income". (3): not for "(a) a quarterly instalment worked out under section 45-112 (on the basis of GDP-adjusted
-- notional tax ...); or (b) an annual instalment, unless it is worked out under paragraph 45-115(1)(a) (based on the Commissioner's
-- rate and your instalment income for the income year)."
@export Must I notify the Commissioner of my instalment income (s 45-20)?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Payer kind` @desc What kind of instalment payer you are
      `my annual instalment uses the Commissioner's rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an annual payer, whether your annual instalment is worked out on the Commissioner's rate and your instalment income
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I notify my instalment income` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a quarterly payer paying 4 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a quarterly payer paying 2 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an annual payer` THEN `my annual instalment uses the Commissioner's rate`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 45-30(1), (2): on assessment (or a nil assessment), a credit equal to "the total of each instalment payable by you for the
-- income year (even if you have not yet paid it); reduced by: the total of each credit that you have claimed under section 45-215
-- or 45-420".
@export What credit do I get for my PAYG instalments (s 45-30)?
GIVEN `instalments payable for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the instalments payable by you for the income year, paid or not, in dollars
      `credits I claimed under ss 45-215, 45-420` IS A NUMBER @desc Credits you claimed under ss 45-215 or 45-420, in dollars
      `I have been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an assessment (or a nil assessment) of your income tax for the year has been made
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What credit do I get for my instalments` MEANS
    IF `I have been assessed` THEN `instalments payable for the year` MINUS `credits I claimed under ss 45-215, 45-420` ELSE 0

§§ `s 45-80; Part IIA ss 8AAC, 8AAD, 8AAE -- the general interest charge if I pay late`

-- s 8AAD(1): "The general interest charge rate for a day is the rate worked out by adding 7 percentage points to the base interest
-- rate for that day, and dividing that total by the number of days in the calendar year." (2): the base interest rate is the
-- Reserve Bank's monthly average yield of 90-day Bank Accepted Bills for a set earlier month -- an INPUT, rounded to 2 decimal
-- places (4).
@export What is the general interest charge rate for a day, in percent (s 8AAD(1))?
GIVEN `the base interest rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The base interest rate for the day under s 8AAD(2), in percent (the 90-day Bank Accepted Bill yield)
      `days in the calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc 365, or 366 in a leap year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the daily general interest charge rate` MEANS
    (`the base interest rate` PLUS 7) DIVIDED BY `days in the calendar year`

-- s 45-80: if you fail to pay an instalment by its due day, you are liable to the general interest charge "on the unpaid amount for
-- each day in the period that: (a) started at the beginning of the day by which the instalment was due to be paid; and (b) finishes
-- at the end of the last day on which ... any of [the instalment or the charge] remains unpaid". s 8AAC(3): the charge for a day is
-- the rate for the day multiplied by "the sum of so much of the following amounts as remains unpaid: (a) the charge from previous
-- days; (b) the original unpaid amount" -- so it compounds daily. s 8AAE: due "at the end of that day". Computed here for a number
-- of days at one rate, nothing paid meanwhile.
GIVEN `unpaid instalment` IS A NUMBER @desc The unpaid instalment, in dollars
      `daily rate in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc The general interest charge rate for each day, in percent
      `days` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days in the period
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the charge accrued` MEANS
    IF `days` AT MOST 0 THEN 0
    ELSE `before` PLUS (`unpaid instalment` PLUS `before`) TIMES `daily rate in percent` DIVIDED BY 100
    WHERE
        `before` MEANS `the charge accrued` `unpaid instalment` `daily rate in percent` (`days` MINUS 1)

-- The result is shown truncated to whole cents: an ENCODER'S CHOICE of display. (s 8AAGA lets the Commissioner round the charge
-- for a period down to a multiple of 5 cents; that is not applied.)
@export How much general interest charge do I owe on a late instalment (ss 45-80, 8AAC, 8AAD)?
GIVEN `unpaid instalment` IS A NUMBER @desc The instalment you did not pay by its due day, in dollars
      `the base interest rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The base interest rate under s 8AAD(2) for the period, in percent
      `days in the calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc 365, or 366 in a leap year
      `days unpaid` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days from the due day to the day you paid, counting both
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much general interest charge do I owe` MEANS
    TRUNC (`the charge accrued` `unpaid instalment`
                                (`What is the daily general interest charge rate` `the base interest rate` `days in the calendar year`)
                                `days unpaid`) 2
